From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abe Massry <amassry@linode.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:34:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] wasi: build QEMU for wasm32-wasi

Teach the build system and QEMU's portability layer about a WASI host:
wasi-sdk's clang targeting wasm32-wasip1, with the module run by a
wasmtime-based host (m-browser).

Build:
- configure: recognise __wasi__ as host_os "wasi"; no CPU_CFLAGS for
  wasm32.
- meson.build: accept wasm32 as a host CPU, and skip the compiler
  version and SafeStack probes for it.  On WASI the only coroutine
  backend is the new "wasi" one; meson_options.txt also gains "fiber",
  the Emscripten backend of the wasm TCG patch.

Portability:
- osdep.h: map sigsetjmp()/siglongjmp() to setjmp()/longjmp() so that
  the compiler emits wasm exception-handling code at each call site
  (wrapper functions break the pairing of jmp_buf and try_table).
  Include the replacement headers from qemu-wasi's wasi-stubs/, and
  provide minimal sigaction and wait-status definitions.  WASI has
  struct iovec, so QEMU's fallback is not used.
- os-posix.h: declare the socket and netdb API that the wasip1 sysroot
  lacks; wasi-stubs/ provides stub implementations.
- os-posix.c, util/osdep.c: no signals, rlimits or mprotect() on WASI.
- util/memalign.c, util/mmap-alloc.c: allocate aligned buffers and
  guest RAM with aligned_alloc(); the emulated mmap() supports neither
  MAP_FIXED nor partial munmap().
- util/event_notifier-posix.c: with no eventfd or pipe, an event
  notifier is a flag, identified by a fake fd number.
- crypto/random-platform.c: use getentropy().
- atomic.h: drop the ATOMIC_REG_SIZE build assertions, as the
  Emscripten patch does.  QEMU uses qatomic_*() on 64-bit fields,
  wider than wasm32's registers; the WASI build is single-threaded.
- util/coroutine-wasi.c: a coroutine backend without stack switching.
  Entering a coroutine calls its entry function directly and a yield
  returns at once.  This works because the WASI build completes I/O
  synchronously (see the following patches).
- include/qemu/wasi-debug.h: WASI_LOG()/WASI_LOG_V() tracing, silent
  unless WASI_DEBUG is 1 (lifecycle) or 2 (also per TB, very verbose);
  no-ops on other hosts.
